    <img src="file:///C:/Users/muhan/.gemini/antigravity/brain/319799a5-9c5c-4fb5-8fba-fbc52878e0b3/end_patrol_modal_1791516467780.jpg" style="max-width: 540pt; border: 1px solid #94a3b8; margin-bottom: 6pt;" /><br>
    <small style="color: #64748b; font-style: italic;">Figure 9.3: Safe Two-Step Patrol Conclusion Modal (Heuristic #5) with Summary & Offline Queue Notice</small>
</div>

<h4>Key Screen Implementations:</h4>
<ol>
    <li><strong>Pre-Patrol Setup Screen:</strong> Live hardware GPS lock (±3.2m), battery reading via <span class="code-inline">navigator.getBattery()</span>, route selection or custom sector route creation.</li>
    <li><strong>Active Patrol Console &amp; Dynamic Vector Map:</strong> Live elapsed timer, Haversine formula distance computation, dynamic SVG map rendering walked GPS breadcrumbs, manual checkpoints, and incident pins.</li>
    <li><strong>Field Incident Reporting Form Modal:</strong> Auto-populates physical coordinates, incident classification (Snare, Poaching, Carcass, etc.), threat severity levels, and real camera file upload with Base64 encoding and thumbnail previews.</li>
    <li><strong>Offline-First Resilience &amp; Batch Sync Engine:</strong> Interactive Online/Offline toggle simulating deep reserve conditions. When offline, records queue in LocalStorage; when online, "Sync Now" transmits a batch payload to <span class="code-inline">/api/patrols/sync</span> with idempotent deduplication.</li>
    <li><strong>Incident Edit &amp; Inspection Table (A2):</strong> Full table of recorded shift incidents with inline editing capabilities before synchronization.</li>
</ol>

<!-- Overview Technologies -->
<h3>Overview: Technologies, Frameworks, and Architecture Used</h3>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Architecture:</strong> Three-Tier Local-First Architecture (Presentation Layer, Application Service Layer, Dual Persistence Layer).</li>
    <li><strong>Frontend:</strong> React 19, Vite, Tailwind CSS, Lucide Icons, HTML5 Geolocation API, FileReader API.</li>
    <li><strong>Backend:</strong> Node.js, Express.js, Mongoose ODM, and local File-System JSON persistence fallback (<span class="code-inline">data/patrols.json</span>, <span class="code-inline">data/incidents.json</span>).</li>
    <li><strong>Design &amp; Quality Practices:</strong> Applied SOLID principles, refactoring techniques, and defensive validation learned in SE3070 lectures.</li>
    <li><strong>Automated Unit Testing:</strong> Jest and Supertest with <strong>87 automated tests passing across 5 test suites (0 failures, &gt;85% code coverage)</strong> verifying patrol lifecycles, Haversine calculations, manual waypoints, incident editing, validation errors, and sync engine deduplication.</li>
</ul>

